# double-stop-sevenths: major sevenths, E string fret N + D string fret N+1
# (recorded as an attempt at tenths with the upper note on the D string instead of the G string).
# Drafted from the recording (envelope onsets + Goertzel harmonic spectrum); confirmed by the bassist.
# Low notes have a weak fundamental (E1 about 7 dB under its 2nd harmonic).
# Each upper note is plucked 0.3-0.5 s after its low note (the dry peak jumps and the
# upper note's partials appear only then), so each chord is two events: the low note
# alone, then both (ticket 12).
timing_tolerance 0.15
cents_tolerance 20

